STIX Two Math (https://github.com/stipub/stixfonts)
Copyright 2001-2021 The STIX Fonts Project Authors (https://github.com/stipub/stixfonts)
License: SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (OFL-1.1)
  - convert/chrome/fonts/STIXTwoMath-Regular.otf is bundled VERBATIM (not
    modified, not recompiled, not pulled from a third-party CDN mirror) so
    convert/'s Chrome-driven PDF/PNG exporters (05-03, 05-04) can render MATH
    glyphs deterministically without any network fetch, matching the same
    self-contained-rendering posture as convert/chrome's other determinism
    guarantees (fixed viewport/timezone/locale, reduced motion). Embedded via
    go:embed and injected as a base64 @font-face data-URI by
    convert/chrome/fonts.go's FontFaceDataURI(), never referenced by a live
    URL. Source: the project's own v2.13 tag,
    fonts/static_otf/STIXTwoMath-Regular.otf (the compiled font binaries are
    not present on the master branch, which .gitignores build output).
  - OFL-1.1 permits verbatim bundling and redistribution; the font's own
    embedded `name` table metadata carries its copyright/license notice
    alongside this NOTICE entry. Reserved Font Name restrictions on
    "STIX Two Math" / "STIX Fonts Project" apply to MODIFIED versions only —
    this repo makes no modification. The .otf binary itself is intentionally
    NOT addlicense-stamped (excluded via -ignore
    'convert/chrome/fonts/**' in the addlicense invocation), matching the
    themes/** precedent for other verbatim-bundled third-party assets above.
  - Full OFL-1.1 text: https://scripts.sil.org/OFL
  - WOFF2 companion (Objective 8, 08-05): convert/chrome/fonts/
    STIXTwoMath-Regular.woff2 is the OFFICIAL stipub/stixfonts WOFF2 build
    for the SAME v2.13 tag as the OTF above (research Open Q4, resolved
    YES — an official build exists, so no local conversion tool was
    needed). Source: https://github.com/stipub/stixfonts, tag v2.13,
    fonts/static_otf_woff2/STIXTwoMath-Regular.woff2 (the WOFF2 sibling of
    the SAME fonts/static_otf/ build family the OTF above is sourced from
    — NOT a third-party CDN mirror, NOT a re-conversion). Fetched verbatim
    via `curl` from raw.githubusercontent.com at that exact tag; not
    modified, not subsetted, not recompiled.
  - MATH-table survival, VERIFIED (not assumed): decompressing this WOFF2
    (`fonttools ttLib.woff2 decompress`) yields an OTF with the identical
    6760-glyph count and the SAME table set as STIXTwoMath-Regular.otf
    (CFF, GDEF, GPOS, GSUB, MATH, OS/2, cmap, head, hhea, hmtx, maxp, name,
    post — the OTF additionally carries a DSIG signature table, which
    stipub's own WOFF2 build process drops, as is conventional for WOFF2
    conversions since the signature does not apply to the transformed
    container; DSIG is not rendering-relevant). convert/chrome/
    fonts_test.go's TestWoff2MathTableSurvivesConversion additionally
    decodes the shipped WOFF2's table directory directly (Go stdlib only,
    per the W3C WOFF2 spec's Known-Table-Tags array) and asserts a MATH
    entry is present, as a standing CI guard against any future
    accidental re-sourcing from a subsetting-prone mirror. convert/chrome/
    fonts_test.go's Chrome-gated TestStixMathTableSmoke goes one step
    further and renders a real MathML stretchy construct through this
    exact WOFF2 via headless Chrome, empirically confirming the MATH
    table's stretchy-construction data is actually consulted (not just
    present in the directory).
  - Embedded via go:embed and exposed as a base64 @font-face data-URI by
    convert/chrome/fonts.go's FontFaceDataURIWoff2() (format('woff2')) —
    additive alongside the existing OTF-based FontFaceDataURI()
    (format('opentype')), which remains unchanged and available.

